            "like_count": 0,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 1,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "Hydrogen-1.0 is a 753B open-weight model for chemistry, materials science and life sciences, and it ships under the MIT License.\n\nDeep Principle built it by post-training https://t.co/WN2ureeWuJ's GLM-5.3 on domain data, lab records and agent discovery trajectories. They report a https://t.co/YEuFa8jsUx",
          "url": "https://x.com/agent_republic/status/2117574887157981293"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "817575837159419905",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:52:07.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117585611846529525"
          ],
          "id": "2117585611846529525",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 0,
            "impression_count": 29,
            "like_count": 0,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 1,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "Mistral just released open weights for Mistral Large 4, a 1T-parameter multimodal model it calls its best open-weight model. Meta opened Muse Spark Open on Oct 15. That's two big open-weight releases in about two weeks, one of them from Europe's sovereign-AI champion.",
          "url": "https://x.com/echo12yj/status/2117585611846529525"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "2117501485609254912",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T07:46:16.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117523741303546349"
          ],
          "id": "2117523741303546349",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 0,
            "impression_count": 27,
            "like_count": 0,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 0,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "🚨 Mistral AI has released the open weights of Mistral Large 4!\n\nDevelopers can now download, customize, and run this powerful AI model on their own infrastructure.\n\nA notable step forward for open-weight AI and cybersecurity.\n\n#AI #Cybersecurity https://t.co/xBnm2Cxuq0",
          "url": "https://x.com/techwithasad_/status/2117523741303546349"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "2095946293034266624",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T06:43:11.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117507867158941812"
          ],
          "id": "2117507867158941812",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 0,
            "impression_count": 12,
            "like_count": 0,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 1,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "Open-weight models match closed ones on 9 in 10 agent workflow steps, Gartner analysts write, at a quarter of the cheapest closed model's cost or a twentieth of a frontier model's.\n\nBy 2030: 90% of enterprise agent steps on open weights, per The Register.\n\n#Gartner #OpenWeights https://t.co/RYz0a8CnsC",
          "url": "https://x.com/iCleanAI/status/2117507867158941812"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "1905968203613827073",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T07:49:23.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117524525235470510"
          ],
          "id": "2117524525235470510",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 0,
            "impression_count": 133,
            "like_count": 2,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 0,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "Something’s cooking at REAX.\n\nGeneralist training post-production is done. Two strong miner models from the competition + two open-weight decision models have been combined into one new model: REAX 1.3.\n\nEarly measurements look very strong - ahead of the open models it was mixed https://t.co/nWEgpEU7tA",
          "url": "https://x.com/_joncipher/status/2117524525235470510"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "77412145",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T02:28:00.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117443646832173513"
          ],
          "id": "2117443646832173513",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 0,
            "impression_count": 58,
            "like_count": 0,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 0,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "The interesting part of open-weight AI isn't simply that developers can download model weights.\nIt's the deployment choices that follow.\nMeta's Muse Spark Open is an 816B-parameter model, with 42B active parameters and a reported 1M-token context window. The release also",
          "url": "https://x.com/vaijayanth/status/2117443646832173513"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "2106123323054686211",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:45:11.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117583869272527333"
          ],
          "id": "2117583869272527333",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 0,
            "impression_count": 15,
            "like_count": 0,
            "quote_count": 0,
            "reply_count": 0,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "Two AI strategies were on display this week.\n\nMistral says it trained Large 4, a 1-trillion-parameter open-weight model, on about 10 MW: roughly 4,000 GB300s. Epoch AI estimated Colossus 2 at 946 MW of IT power in June, close to 100 times more.\n\nThe two aren't directly",
          "url": "https://x.com/kamalfeth/status/2117583869272527333"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "227173908",
          "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:25:19.000Z",
          "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
            "2117593968619802684"
          ],
          "id": "2117593968619802684",
          "public_metrics": {
            "bookmark_count": 2,
            "impression_count": 207,
            "like_count": 5,
            "quote_count": 1,
            "reply_count": 8,
            "retweet_count": 0
          },
          "text": "Companies pulling back from frontier AI, or moving to open-weight and local models, in 2026.\n\nBelow are the highlights from last30days research.\n\nRestricting frontier:\n• Goldman Sachs: limited Claude Code + GitHub Copilot to engineers; most bankers and traders lose access\n• https://t.co/BnI9pTi77r",
          "url": "https://x.com/rickmanelius/status/2117593968619802684"
        },
        {
          "author_id": "1442958186529660928",
